 ## Overview
-A technique using contours to separate portions of a volume before transfer function (FT) specification, allowing manual specification on the isolated region [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sketch-based methods by using explicit geometric boundaries (contours) to define regions of interest, whereas sketch-based methods rely on neural networks to interpret freehand strokes [S1, unofficial].
+This method uses user-drawn contours to isolate specific portions of a volume before transfer function (FT) specification, allowing for manual parameter definition on the isolated region [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods by replacing complex topological tree traversal or neural network training with direct geometric separation via 2D sketches [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and outputs:**
-- Input: A scalar volume dataset $V$.
-- Output: A transfer function $T$ defined specifically for the isolated region.
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+- Input: A 3D volume dataset, a 2D slice or projection view of the volume, and user-drawn 2D contours.
+- Output: A transfer function (FT) defined for the region enclosed by the contours.
 
